    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## Before the demo

      The history tool creates missing memory tables and configuration on
      first use, copies new Agent questions with their answers, and embeds a
      bounded batch. The first request can be slower because it makes one
      provider call per newly indexed question. A dedicated test
      notebook can validate question-to-answer pairing, semantic matches,
      dates, RUN_IDs, and both team definitions without changing this file.

      Oracle references:
      - https://docs.oracle.com/en/cloud/paas/autonomous-database/serverless/adbsb/dbms-cloud-ai-agent-views-history.html
      - https://docs.oracle.com/en/database/oracle/oracle-database/26/vecse/utl_to_embedding-and-utl_to_embeddings-dbms_vector.html
      - https://docs.oracle.com/en/database/oracle/oracle-database/26/sqlrf/vector_distance.html
    languageId: markdown
